course: dictionary
lesson: 1051
title: A word from the kitchen: borshch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Borshch is a word from Ukrainian, the language of Ukraine. It is the Ukrainian spelling, in Latin letters, of the word «borscht». Say it as «borshch», with the «shch» sounds run together, like «fresh cheese».
explain: The words around a new word are its context, and they leave clues. «borshch is a red beetroot soup served with sour cream.» Red, beetroot, soup and sour cream all point to food. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A soup, and it is a red one.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Lunch at Granny's often starts with a red beetroot soup with sour cream» still makes sense, so the meaning is right. If your meaning does not fit the sentence, go back and look at the clues again.
fact: Borshch is a sour beetroot soup and a national dish of Ukraine.
fact: Borshch often has beetroot, cabbage, potatoes and sometimes meat.
fact: Borshch is often served with sour cream, garlic bread (pampushky) and dill.
fact: «smetAna» means sour cream, and it is sour, not sweet like whipped cream.
fact: «dvanAdtsyat strav» means the twelve dishes of the Christmas Eve supper, and they are meatless.
exercise: «borshch is a red beetroot soup served with sour cream.» What is borshch? | A sweet cake with poppy seeds | *A red beetroot soup | A sort of bread
exercise: «Lunch at Granny's often starts with borshch, a red beetroot soup with a spoon of smetAna, sour cream.» What is smetAna? | Dill | *Sour cream | Garlic bread | Whipped cream, sweet and light
exercise: Which of these is not usually in borshch? | Beetroot | Potatoes | *Chocolate sauce | Cabbage
test: «dvanAdtsyat strav» is the Christmas Eve supper with twelve dishes. What does dvanAdtsyat strav mean? | A soup for breakfast | Twelve pieces of bread | A summer picnic | *The twelve dishes of the Christmas Eve supper
test: «In 2022 UNESCO listed the culture of Ukrainian borshch cooking as heritage in need of urgent protection.» What did UNESCO do in 2022? | *Listed Ukrainian borshch cooking as heritage needing urgent protection | Made borshch a sweet dessert | Banned borshch from schools | Opened a borshch shop in Paris
exam: You meet borshch in a text about Ukraine and do not know it. What is the best strategy? | *Read the words around it, then swap in your meaning to check it still fits | Guess it is a dance because it sounds fun | Skip the word forever and never think about it again
